These files are only in the source directory, as the binary distribution
is not intended to be modified directly. You would have to download the
source code archive and recreate the files from there. The tiles do not
depend on a specific operating system.

>My apologies, I was refering to the Slash'em tile32.

In Slash'EM, it might be a different location (the tiles I referred to
above are actually NetHack's 16-tiles). 

Your best bet is to download the source code; even if you end up not
recompiling, just the sequential list of monsters saves you some trouble.
